      "raw": "[quote=\"Melonball\"]\n\nIf a card says &quot;deal 1 damage to a target, cards dealt damage in this way suffer X effect&quot; is dealing the damage enough to trigger the effect? &nbsp;Or dies the target have to take damage after reduction is applied.I used to think that the target had to take damage to trigger the effect, but there&#39;s a mr fixer card that&#39;s worded to specifically reference &quot;taking damage&quot; as opposed to &quot;dealt&quot; so I was unsure.thanks!\n\n[/quote]\n\n&nbsp;\n\nIn the example you have given it does in fact have to take damage after any reduction to trigger the effect. There are some cards that don&#39;t have to deal damage, such as Wraith&#39;s Stun Bolt &quot;The Wraith deals 1 target 1 Projectile damage. Until the start of your next turn, reduce all damage dealt by 1.&quot; as it doesn&#39;t have the &quot;cards dealt damage&quot; clause in it. Now Throat Jab on the other hand reads &#39;The target dealt damage this way cannot deal damage until the start of your next turn.&quot; Will have to deal damage.\n",
